Package: ggmtools
Title: Shared Tools for Multiple Gaussian Graphical Model Packages
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Margaret", "Janiczek", , "mjaniczek@umass.edu", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")),
    person("Raji", "Balasubramanian", , "rbalasub@umass.edu", role = "aut")
  )
Description: Generics, evaluation metrics and data shared by packages that
    estimate multiple Gaussian graphical models, such as 'spikeyglass' and
    'multiGGM'. Provides a common long edge-table format with generics to
    extract posterior inclusion probabilities and partial-correlation
    estimates from fitted models; receiver operating characteristic (ROC)
    and precision-recall curves that handle tied scores correctly;
    confusion metrics at a threshold; estimation losses; Bayesian false
    discovery rate selection and pooled permutation p-values; matrix and
    edge-table utilities; and a breast-cancer gene-expression dataset for
    the phosphoinositide 3-kinase (PI3K) pathway from The Cancer Genome
    Atlas (TCGA). Methods include the direct posterior probability approach
    to false discovery rates of Newton et al. (2004)
    <doi:10.1093/biostatistics/5.2.155>, the precision-recall interpolation
    of Davis and Goadrich (2006) <doi:10.1145/1143844.1143874>, and a
    Bayesian information criterion for tuning the joint graphical lasso of
    Danaher et al. (2014) <doi:10.1111/rssb.12033>.
